WEBVTT

00:05.984 --> 00:12.004
[Carl Jung, Psychology and Alchemy]

00:16.505 --> 00:19.519
- I have a bad feeling about this.
- Who are you gonna invite?

00:19.520 --> 00:19.887
- Who are you gonna invite?

00:19.927 --> 00:23.285
So, you know how we're giving
each other our positive votes?

00:23.310 --> 00:24.017
Shh!

00:24.041 --> 00:27.356
Let's not discuss that in the classroom.

00:32.341 --> 00:34.942
Damn, the vibes in here are toxic.

00:36.200 --> 00:40.040
Ugh, is it gonna be like this until voting day?

00:43.896 --> 00:48.020
It seems everyone's set on keeping
their heads down until after the vote.

00:48.279 --> 00:53.645
Either that, or forming groups to protect
each other with their positive votes.

00:54.818 --> 00:58.208
Is there really no other way?

00:58.654 --> 01:02.591
I thought you were prepared
to let someone be expelled.

01:02.739 --> 01:05.552
Suddenly you sound like Ryuuen.

01:05.943 --> 01:11.645
For someone who accused Ryuuen of bluffing,
you don't seem that confident yourself.

01:11.794 --> 01:12.817
What are you…?!

01:13.154 --> 01:16.809
So, what are you planning to do?

01:17.075 --> 01:18.762
I…

01:19.840 --> 01:23.496
The reason I can't support
the class the way I want to

01:23.863 --> 01:26.699
is because I lack the resolve
required of a leader.

01:29.676 --> 01:33.684
My brother… how am I supposed to face him?

03:17.548 --> 03:18.990
If you're free this evening,

03:19.196 --> 03:20.751
can we meet at the dorms?

03:21.501 --> 03:23.352
I'd like to talk to you.

03:26.642 --> 03:28.759
Hey, Ayanokouji!

03:30.587 --> 03:31.696
Headed home?

03:32.025 --> 03:33.548
Asahina.

03:34.344 --> 03:36.446
You're not hanging with Honami today?

03:36.728 --> 03:40.626
Ichinose and I aren't that close.

03:40.743 --> 03:44.868
Are you sure?
She said herself that you're friends.

03:45.040 --> 03:46.813
Do you need something?

03:47.056 --> 03:50.282
You're no fun. Well, whatever.

03:51.212 --> 03:55.719
There's something you should know
about our precious little Honami.

03:56.938 --> 04:00.282
Apparently, she asked that Miyabi guy

04:01.415 --> 04:04.118
for his help on the exam.

04:04.923 --> 04:06.538
She went to President Nagumo?

04:06.861 --> 04:12.446
She asked him for the extra points she needs
to get 200,000 to reverse an expulsion.

04:13.157 --> 04:16.226
So, what do you think Miyabi said to that?

04:16.493 --> 04:19.719
I'm guessing he drove a hard bargain?

04:20.548 --> 04:24.235
He said he'd do it on one condition…

04:25.181 --> 04:27.407
She has to date him.

04:28.595 --> 04:31.907
Should you really be telling me this?

04:32.407 --> 04:34.548
I'm doing it for my class.

04:35.243 --> 04:41.493
If he lends all those points to a first-year,
it'll hang over our heads for ages.

04:41.891 --> 04:43.071
And more importantly…

04:43.993 --> 04:50.587
I feel bad for Honami, going to
all that trouble to protect us.

04:51.697 --> 04:54.048
But why are you telling me?

04:54.118 --> 04:55.391
I dunno, really!

04:55.420 --> 04:59.102
It just seems like you might
be able to do something.

05:00.118 --> 05:00.969
I guess…

05:02.361 --> 05:06.173
you could call it a Hail Mary or whatever?

05:07.111 --> 05:11.579
Anyway, now you know. Ball's in your court.

05:22.978 --> 05:26.071
Sorry, I hate to take up so much of your time.

05:26.595 --> 05:28.360
Don't worry about it.

05:29.822 --> 05:33.735
I don't want to make you stand here,
so why don't we go to my dorm?

05:40.782 --> 05:42.735
Well, fancy meeting you here…

05:43.142 --> 05:46.110
Hirata and Ayanokouji, my boys.

05:46.361 --> 05:47.469
Kouenji.

05:47.736 --> 05:52.923
Well now, keep your eyes on the prize
and give the exam your all!

05:54.220 --> 05:56.266
You seem unfazed.

05:56.353 --> 05:59.149
One little extra exam can't faze me.

05:59.673 --> 06:05.884
Throw out the trash that's slowing us down,
and we'll pick ourselves back up and move on!

06:13.509 --> 06:15.712
Ayanokouji. Let's go.

06:15.892 --> 06:16.743
Yeah.

06:22.415 --> 06:24.477
Our first year is almost over.

06:25.681 --> 06:31.469
A deserted island, that brutal training camp…
an eventful year, to say the least.

06:31.845 --> 06:34.508
Yeah, but it was fun in a way.

06:35.165 --> 06:39.844
The class has come together much more than
I thought we could in the beginning, too.

06:39.970 --> 06:40.954
Yeah.

06:41.368 --> 06:44.954
But then… this exam has really
thrown a wrench in it.

06:45.853 --> 06:48.008
Is that what you wanted to talk about?

06:48.040 --> 06:53.985
Sorry, I just can't think of any
solid strategy at all this time.

06:55.032 --> 06:58.032
No matter how hard I try…

06:59.267 --> 07:03.462
It just doesn't seem possible to save everyone.

07:04.345 --> 07:06.102
Sorry, I don't know, either.

07:06.493 --> 07:12.040
Realistically, we probably can't scrape together
200,000 points to reverse an expulsion.

07:12.978 --> 07:14.454
You're probably right.

07:15.017 --> 07:18.727
This exam is forcing us to get rid of
someone we don't need.

07:19.321 --> 07:23.594
But Hirata will never be able to decide
who that "someone" should be.

07:23.806 --> 07:26.118
Hey, Ayanokouji…

07:27.251 --> 07:31.118
Is there anyone in particular
you think should be expelled?

07:31.993 --> 07:33.719
Not really.

07:33.962 --> 07:37.540
Whoever we lose, we'll all just have to accept it.

07:38.462 --> 07:44.008
That's a logical approach. You'd make
a way better class leader than me.

07:44.400 --> 07:46.633
That's going way too far.

07:47.681 --> 07:54.508
Be as humble as you want, but I've thought so
ever since the thing with Karuizawa.

07:59.907 --> 08:02.876
Sorry for calling you so late.

08:03.579 --> 08:04.891
Don't worry about it!

08:05.157 --> 08:09.188
But I was pretty surprised to hear from you.

08:10.657 --> 08:13.555
There's something I wanted to discuss in person.

08:13.876 --> 08:17.337
The floor's cold, so have a seat on the bed.

08:17.407 --> 08:18.998
Oh, thank you.

08:23.009 --> 08:25.751
I feel kind of nervous for some reason.

08:26.009 --> 08:27.430
About the exam.

08:27.884 --> 08:29.798
What was your plan again?

08:30.086 --> 08:35.648
Hmm… I guess I'm trying to
make sure no one gets expelled.

08:36.318 --> 08:40.749
I thought you'd gone to President Nagumo for help.

08:41.419 --> 08:42.662
What kind of help?

08:43.100 --> 08:47.802
Even Class B can't possibly have 200,000 points.

08:48.600 --> 08:53.279
Meaning, you'd have no choice
but to enlist a third party.

08:53.802 --> 08:56.950
I get it… Asahina must have told you.

08:57.295 --> 08:59.967
So, do you know the conditions I agreed to, too?

09:00.326 --> 09:01.114
Yeah.

09:01.685 --> 09:05.185
It's silly, isn't it? In more ways than one.

09:06.880 --> 09:07.922
Thank you.

09:09.201 --> 09:11.091
How many points did you need?

09:11.748 --> 09:15.036
A little over 40,000 or so.

09:15.432 --> 09:17.432
It's hard to say no to that.

09:18.053 --> 09:25.763
Yeah, I don't know why he would give
all of those points just to go out with me.

09:26.396 --> 09:30.521
Honestly, it would make more sense
for him to charge me for the privilege.

09:31.092 --> 09:37.068
I think if I want to keep everyone
in Class B safe, this is the only way.

09:37.646 --> 09:38.755
I see.

09:40.584 --> 09:42.761
You don't think less of me now?

09:42.786 --> 09:44.763
I have no reason to.

09:45.287 --> 09:50.630
I don't understand why you'd go
that far just to save one person, though.

09:51.771 --> 09:55.404
Did you call me because you were
worried about me, by any chance?

09:56.131 --> 09:59.513
Maybe that was presumptuous of me.

09:59.717 --> 10:02.958
Not at all! That makes me really happy!

10:03.434 --> 10:04.535
But…

10:05.529 --> 10:07.482
this does make it a little harder.

10:09.335 --> 10:15.323
If I hadn't talked to you about it, I think
I might've felt braver about my decision.

10:21.031 --> 10:26.139
Hey, Ayanokouji… you're more
impressive than you let on, aren't you?

10:26.343 --> 10:28.624
Not as far as I know, sorry.

10:28.694 --> 10:30.922
If you're unaware of it, that's amazing!

10:31.015 --> 10:33.015
I mean, Ayanokouji, you're…

10:35.421 --> 10:36.561
What?

10:38.609 --> 10:41.304
No, never mind.

10:42.632 --> 10:44.108
What can I say?

10:49.475 --> 10:51.499
Are you serious right now?

10:51.624 --> 10:54.507
- Come on, would I lie to you?
- Wanna go with me?

10:56.526 --> 10:57.953
Did something happen?

10:57.978 --> 10:59.701
I was wondering the same thing.

11:00.174 --> 11:01.885
Something doesn't seem right.

11:02.690 --> 11:05.081
Everyone was so on edge yesterday.

11:05.870 --> 11:07.189
And now, suddenly…

11:10.041 --> 11:15.682
They must have put together a new group
and agreed to take someone down.

11:18.198 --> 11:19.518
You're probably right.

11:19.752 --> 11:23.439
Now that you mention it,
it seems that way to me, too.

11:23.596 --> 11:26.129
Then, should one of us do reconnaissance?

11:26.154 --> 11:30.380
No, anyone who goes sniffing around
might end up with a target on their back.

11:30.405 --> 11:31.482
But what if…

11:31.557 --> 11:35.486
someone in our group is already the target?

11:35.799 --> 11:38.275
D-Don't say that, Haruka!

11:38.330 --> 11:42.689
No one has invited any of us to join
a group, so we can't rule it out.

11:43.198 --> 11:47.916
If they threaten to aim for one of us if we
don't do what they say, what's our plan?

11:48.135 --> 11:50.978
We have to stay loyal to each other!

11:51.127 --> 11:54.611
Even if that makes one of us a target?

11:54.674 --> 11:55.994
Well…

11:56.815 --> 12:01.338
Staying at this school isn't important
enough to make me sell out a friend.

12:01.401 --> 12:04.424
I'd never betray any of you, either!

12:05.104 --> 12:06.252
And you, Keisei?

12:07.752 --> 12:11.236
I agree with what you're saying,
on a fundamental level.

12:11.370 --> 12:13.808
But life isn't always fair.

12:14.307 --> 12:17.654
Getting expelled to protect a friend
certainly sounds noble,

12:18.002 --> 12:19.955
but that's easier said than done.

12:27.893 --> 12:29.619
Hirata…

12:37.702 --> 12:38.594
What is it?

12:38.619 --> 12:40.540
I've got, like, majorly bad news.

12:41.087 --> 12:44.517
Everyone is saying you're gonna be
the one who gets expelled.

12:45.924 --> 12:47.126
I see.

12:47.934 --> 12:52.939
[Classroom of the Elite
3rd Season]

12:53.736 --> 12:55.692
What, is that it?!

12:55.759 --> 12:56.978
Did you know already?

12:57.041 --> 12:58.962
No, not until now.

12:59.048 --> 13:01.009
Then why the heck are you so calm?!

13:01.307 --> 13:04.307
Do you know how many people are voting against me?

13:04.688 --> 13:09.657
Let me think… I'd say it's probably
almost half the class at this point.

13:09.706 --> 13:11.706
Well, that's inconvenient.

13:11.853 --> 13:13.853
So, like, what the heck do we do?

13:14.041 --> 13:17.001
I mean, you can stop this somehow, right?

13:17.088 --> 13:19.174
I'll have to think it over.

13:20.595 --> 13:22.939
You gotta get with the program.

13:22.969 --> 13:27.251
Without me, they would've
kicked you out just like that!

13:27.494 --> 13:30.247
And that's exactly why I need you.

13:30.701 --> 13:32.396
Oh, right…

13:32.614 --> 13:34.793
This is good information.

13:35.146 --> 13:36.958
Thanks, Kei.

13:38.062 --> 13:40.452
Y-Yeah, you'd better be grateful.

13:40.671 --> 13:42.522
I'll be in touch again soon.

13:42.828 --> 13:44.600
Sure, got it.

13:46.578 --> 13:49.180
Does he know what he's doing?

13:53.531 --> 13:58.616
I had a feeling I might be
hearing from you tonight.

13:58.788 --> 14:01.833
I want to know who pointed
everyone in my direction.

14:02.006 --> 14:06.341
Sorry, but I couldn't tell you
even if I wanted to.

14:06.701 --> 14:11.810
The identity of the person behind this
is for my ears only, you see.

14:12.615 --> 14:14.341
I see how it is.

14:14.568 --> 14:18.326
You're sharp, Ayanokouji. I knew you'd understand.

14:18.592 --> 14:21.638
I assume whoever it is came to you first,

14:21.989 --> 14:24.465
and used your connections

14:24.639 --> 14:27.896
to get everyone who's not
already on my side on board.

14:28.006 --> 14:31.185
This isn't easy for me, you know?

14:31.271 --> 14:34.630
It's not like I want you expelled,

14:34.756 --> 14:38.763
but when someone's counting on me,
I just can't bear to let them down.

14:39.466 --> 14:41.990
You're not gonna tell me anything, then, huh.

14:42.240 --> 14:44.544
Sorry for bothering you so late at night.

14:44.763 --> 14:47.442
Wow, I didn't think you'd give up so easily.

14:47.568 --> 14:50.185
Do you think you can figure it out by yourself?

14:50.240 --> 14:52.974
We'll see. I'm not getting my hopes up.

14:53.144 --> 14:54.675
Hmm…

14:56.714 --> 14:59.190
Okay! I'll tell you.

15:00.206 --> 15:02.510
It was Yamauchi's idea.

15:03.691 --> 15:05.018
Interesting.

15:05.566 --> 15:06.971
Are you happy now?

15:07.464 --> 15:10.576
It wasn't him, it was Sakayanagi.

15:12.839 --> 15:15.221
Figured it out, did you?

15:15.691 --> 15:21.518
I don't think you'd take on the risk it takes
to be the middleman on Yamauchi's orders.

15:22.495 --> 15:26.784
And Sakayanagi came to see Yamauchi the other day.

15:27.277 --> 15:31.667
I'd hate to make an enemy
of someone like Sakayanagi.

15:32.238 --> 15:34.340
Thanks for your help, Kushida.

15:34.620 --> 15:38.378
Tread carefully, now.
Good luck not getting expelled!

15:49.292 --> 15:50.120
What is it?

15:50.456 --> 15:52.839
I want you to do something for me.

15:54.269 --> 15:56.487
Understood. I'll get to work tomorrow.

15:56.792 --> 15:57.846
Thanks.

16:10.011 --> 16:13.014
[From: Horikita Manabu]
[To: Horikita Suzune]
[Are you sure you'll have no regrets?]

16:22.887 --> 16:24.488
I'm sorry I'm late.

16:25.652 --> 16:28.894
How long has it been since we last spoke alone?

16:29.277 --> 16:31.464
Aside from after the entrance ceremony,

16:31.785 --> 16:33.503
it's been three years now.

16:33.668 --> 16:36.457
I see. I had a feeling it was something like that.

16:39.498 --> 16:44.808
If you're here to ask for points for the
supplemental exam, you're wasting your time.

16:44.902 --> 16:45.933
I'm not.

16:46.340 --> 16:51.738
It never would have occurred to me
to ask for that kind of help.

16:54.418 --> 16:58.168
I'm here to ask you for courage.

16:59.980 --> 17:04.198
At the moment, everyone is trying to
stay under the radar until the exam,

17:04.598 --> 17:08.550
or forming groups in a desperate attempt
to control the voting results.

17:09.395 --> 17:15.199
I'm simply avoiding the overwhelming pressure
to choose a candidate for expulsion myself.

17:16.458 --> 17:20.042
If I keep doing that, I know
I'll come to regret it one day.

17:21.028 --> 17:24.848
So, I've decided to face it.

17:25.332 --> 17:29.957
I want to confront this exam head-on, and
find a solution I can make peace with.

17:32.637 --> 17:34.348
I have one question for you.

17:34.660 --> 17:36.495
What do you think of this school?

17:36.520 --> 17:37.207
Huh?

17:37.278 --> 17:38.590
Do you enjoy it here?

17:39.028 --> 17:40.879
Ah, well…

17:42.130 --> 17:44.560
Forgive me. I…

17:45.223 --> 17:48.544
honestly can't say whether I enjoy it or not.

17:49.325 --> 17:52.129
All I can say is that I don't find it boring.

17:52.707 --> 17:53.769
I see.

17:54.325 --> 17:57.887
So you've overcome one of your weaknesses.

17:59.082 --> 18:01.644
You were once unaware of the world around you.

18:02.293 --> 18:07.629
Now that you've broadened your horizons,
you're beginning to escape the tedium.

18:08.473 --> 18:11.441
I didn't expect to hear this from you.

18:11.817 --> 18:13.707
What did you expect to hear?

18:14.047 --> 18:18.601
You see no value in anything
other than grades and reputation.

18:18.727 --> 18:22.242
That's because… I've always aimed

18:22.641 --> 18:24.789
to measure up to you.

18:25.133 --> 18:26.640
So that's your goal.

18:27.547 --> 18:31.281
Then, how do you view Ayanokouji?

18:32.094 --> 18:34.546
As a classmate of no consequence to me.

18:35.094 --> 18:39.765
Although, I also see him as someone
to catch up to and surpass someday.

18:39.967 --> 18:43.623
I'm afraid you'll never catch up to him.

18:44.913 --> 18:47.654
Still, you have no need to.

18:48.460 --> 18:51.115
You should find your own way to grow.

18:51.397 --> 18:53.162
My own way?

18:57.670 --> 18:58.795
Does that scare you?

18:59.686 --> 19:01.686
Yes, it does.

19:02.163 --> 19:07.139
If you want to close the gap, you must
start with a single step forward.

19:08.171 --> 19:09.701
How do I do that?

19:10.278 --> 19:14.285
You lack experience now, but you
will find the answer to that in time.

19:15.496 --> 19:21.012
So, will you tell me what it is
that you plan to say to your class?

19:23.661 --> 19:24.911
Yes.

19:28.520 --> 19:31.012
The supplemental exam is tomorrow.

19:31.309 --> 19:33.801
Make sure you don't oversleep and miss it.

19:34.004 --> 19:36.754
Who would be stupid enough to do that?

19:36.825 --> 19:37.676
Anyone?

19:38.121 --> 19:39.504
Class is dismissed.

19:40.067 --> 19:42.613
It's not like Yamauchi has the wrong idea.

19:42.864 --> 19:49.769
It's just unfortunate that I'm the one
Sakayanagi smooth-talked him into targeting.

19:50.848 --> 19:53.316
Well… it's your move, Horikita.

19:54.137 --> 19:57.168
You should be able to handle it by now.

20:00.450 --> 20:02.473
Excuse me, everyone.

20:03.074 --> 20:04.988
May I have a moment of your time?

20:07.153 --> 20:09.340
What is it, Horikita?

20:09.637 --> 20:13.762
I have something to say about the vote tomorrow.

20:13.787 --> 20:15.670
Huh? Why now?

20:16.466 --> 20:18.216
What is there to say?

20:18.365 --> 20:22.060
Kanji and I already have plans.

20:22.255 --> 20:27.107
You're taking this a little too lightly,
considering someone may be expelled tomorrow.

20:27.318 --> 20:29.318
W-Well, I just…

20:29.592 --> 20:31.849
already prepared myself for that, okay?

20:32.263 --> 20:34.263
Your fortitude is admirable,

20:34.435 --> 20:38.287
but this is something I need
the entire class to hear.

20:39.600 --> 20:43.108
For the past few days, I've been
thinking everything over.

20:43.420 --> 20:47.068
Who should stay, and who should go.

20:47.553 --> 20:51.794
And today, the answer finally became clear to me.

20:52.068 --> 20:54.185
I'd like to share that with you now.

20:54.217 --> 20:55.460
Wait, Horikita.

20:55.646 --> 20:58.013
We can't afford to lose anyone here.

20:58.201 --> 21:00.466
Please allow me to finish.

21:01.068 --> 21:03.224
I've had my doubts from the beginning.

21:03.708 --> 21:07.599
This exam didn't establish a structure
for us to discuss it as a class.

21:07.966 --> 21:12.083
That can only lead to a battle to form
groups in order to control the vote.

21:12.154 --> 21:13.360
That's true.

21:13.475 --> 21:19.849
As such, there's a risk that even an exemplary
student might be the one expelled in the end.

21:20.178 --> 21:22.904
You can hardly call that an exam.

21:23.185 --> 21:28.232
I'm not sure what's gotten into you, but
you're speaking like a whole new woman.

21:28.818 --> 21:30.460
Let's hear it, then.

21:30.786 --> 21:32.887
What would you have us do?

21:33.295 --> 21:37.107
In a perfect world, we would all
discuss who to expel as a class.

21:37.216 --> 21:39.611
But that's hardly realistic at this point.

21:39.826 --> 21:40.826
Therefore…

21:41.889 --> 21:45.232
I ask you to allow me to designate
who should be expelled.

21:47.115 --> 21:49.911
We can't! It'll just cause more disagreements!

21:50.053 --> 21:52.357
We could at least hear her out.

21:52.553 --> 21:55.099
The redhead has a point.

21:56.422 --> 22:01.203
I've decided that if someone
has to be expelled for this exam…

22:03.297 --> 22:05.219
Yamauchi Haruki.

22:08.672 --> 22:09.867
It should be you.
